Task: Refine ONLY the iOS live audio visualization behavior during voice recording.

The actual recording and transcription flow is now working correctly end-to-end.

Do NOT modify the transcription pipeline, backend upload, audio file format handling, API endpoint, recorder lifecycle, or any web code.

This task is ONLY about the visual behavior of the live recording bars in the iOS composer.

⸻

CURRENT PROBLEM

The current visualization starts from an empty center area and gradually creates/fills bars over time.

That is not the behavior I want.

I want the visualization to behave more like a continuous live audio stream:

* the entire available visualization area should already be filled from the first moment;
* all bars/dots should already exist when recording begins;
* they should continuously move/flow;
* voice should change their height and brightness, not create them from nothing.

In other words:

Do not build the waveform progressively from empty space.

The visual field must be present immediately.

⸻

DESIRED INITIAL STATE

The instant the user taps the microphone and recording mode becomes active:

the full horizontal area between the Cancel button and Stop button should already contain many small blue rounded bars/dots.

No waiting.

No empty space that slowly fills.

No “bar 1 appears, then bar 2, then bar 3 until the row is full.”

The row should be visually complete from the very first frame.

Think of it as a continuous moving conveyor of small audio dots.

⸻

IDLE / SILENCE BEHAVIOR

When the microphone hears little or no sound:

* all bars remain very short;
* they should look almost like small rounded dots/dashes;
* their blue color should be darker / lower-opacity;
* they should continue moving/flowing horizontally;
* the animation should remain alive even during silence.

Silence should NOT freeze the visualization.

Silence means:

small + dark + subtle movement

not:

no visualization

⸻

VOICE REACTION

When the user speaks:

the bars currently passing through the visualization should react to the real microphone amplitude.

Voice should affect TWO visual properties:

1. Height

quieter speech → slightly taller bars
normal speech → medium height
louder speech → taller bars

2. Brightness / opacity

quiet/silence → darker BlueMind blue
active speech → brighter / clearer BlueMind blue

The stronger the voice, the brighter and taller the active bars should become.

This brightness transition is important.

I want the user to immediately feel:

“the microphone is hearing me.”

⸻

COLOR

Use BlueMind blue for the visualization.

Do not use white as the primary bar color.

Use one BlueMind-blue family with intensity variation:

* silence: darker/lower-opacity blue;
* speech: brighter/more visible blue.

Do not use rainbow colors.

Do not introduce multiple unrelated colors.

Keep the style minimal and premium.

⸻

MOVEMENT MODEL

The bars/dots should continuously progress horizontally.

But the full visualization window must always remain filled.

Conceptually:

there is a fixed number of visible bars.

Every update:

* a new sample enters from one side;
* the oldest sample leaves from the other side;
* the whole row remains visually full.

Do NOT start with an empty array and append until full.

Initialize the buffer immediately with silent/default samples.

Example concept:

At recording start:

••••••••••••••••••••••••••••

During speech:

•••▪▮▌▪••••▏▮▌▪••••••••••••

while the sequence continuously moves.

⸻

